```ts
type Result<T> =
  | { ok: true; value: T }
  | { ok: false; error: ApiError }

const res = await fetchUser(id)
if (!res.ok) return showError(res.error)
render(res.value)
```

No `try`/`catch` at call sites. TypeScript flags an unhandled error branch.

```ts
try {
  render(await fetchUser(id))
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof ApiError) showError(e)
  else throw e
}
```

Shortest happy path, but nothing forces callers to catch.

```ts
fetchUser(id, (err, user) => {
  if (err) return showError(err)
  render(user)
})
```

Only worth it if you need to support the old plugin API.
